# From "Intro Focus 25" (Wave VII - Voyager, CD2-3): a fuller account of F25
# than briefing-f25.gws's few lines -- explicit about visiting without
# participating, and that the size of a belief's territory tracks how many
# hold it, down to the smallest.

@segment  focus-25-observation
@title    Focus 25 — Visiting Without Participation
@levels   F25
@duration ~3m

say Before you and around you are the expressions of every human belief about existence beyond time and space.
pause 8
say The more people who hold a given belief, the stronger its presence here. But even the smallest is real too -- held up by no more than a few.
pause 8
say You remain calm and conscious. You're here to observe, not to participate.
pause 6
say You may recognize people you know. You're only a visitor here -- here to observe, and to remember, and to carry the memory back with you.
pause 8
say Go and explore now, as a visitor. Take in the perspective this freedom gives you.
hold 90
